    <div class="wprm-recipe-summary wprm-block-text-normal"><span style="display: block;"><strong>Serves:</strong> 8 | <strong>Dietary:</strong> Vegetarian, Nut-Free | <strong>Make Ahead:</strong> Assemble the day before and bake in the morning</span><div class="wprm-spacer"></div><span style="display: block;">Bread pudding with goat cheese is an unexpected combination, but the tang cuts through the sweetness, balancing every bite. The berries soften and bleed into the custard as it bakes, which is exactly the look you want on a brunch spread.</span><div class="wprm-spacer"></div><span style="display: block;">I use a soft day-old bread like brioche or <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/challah-bread-recipe/">challah</a>. I add a few extra egg yolks to the batter for the creamiest custard. A dollop of cr&egrave;me fra&icirc;che rounds it out when serving. </span></div>
